<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19868970</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2130932</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>CALCIUM AND PHOSPHORUS METABOLISM IN OSTEOMALACIA</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Miles</surname><given-names>Lee Monroe</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>Chih-Tung</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x1c01e30N0x3c4bf98">From the Departments of Obstetrics and Gynecology and of Pharmacology of the Peking Union Medical College, Peking, China.</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>1</month><year>1925</year></pub-date><volume>41</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>137</fpage><lpage>157</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>24</day><month>8</month><year>1924</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; Copyright, 1925, by The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research New York</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> Osteomalacia is a diet deficiency disease of the same category as rickets. The deficiency is principally in the fat-soluble vitamine content of the diet, though there may be a calcium deficiency at the same time. The disease may be prevented by providing a diet rich in the fat-soluble vitamine content, and may be cured by adding the same to the diet. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>